digraph G {
  rankdir=LR;
  node [shape=box];
  "main.initCache" [tooltip="File: main.go:105\n\nThis function initializes a cache database by opening a SQLite database connection at the specified directory, creating a table to store explanations, and returning a Cache struct instance tied to this database connection upon successful setup."];
  "astVisitor.getFunctionName" [tooltip="File: main.go:251\n\nThis function returns the fully qualified name of an AST function declaration, combining the package name with the function name. If the function has a receiver, it appends the receiver type name to the package name before adding the function name. The receiver type name is obtained from a separate function call, which is assumed to be implemented elsewhere."];
  "astVisitor.getReceiver" [tooltip="File: main.go:259\n\nThis function returns the receiver name of an AST-generated function declaration, or an empty string if no receiver is declared, by inspecting the first field in the receiver struct and determining its type and name."];
  "astVisitor.getCallTarget" [tooltip="File: main.go:276\n\nThis function determines the target of a call expression in an abstract syntax tree, and returns it as a string. It supports calls to named fields, methods, and identifiers, prioritizing the current type when applicable and inferring types from variable names for complex expressions. The result is constructed by prefixing the name of the target field or method with the namespace formed by the package name and the current or inferred type."];
  "main.inferTypeFromVarName" [tooltip="File: main.go:305\n\nThis function determines the inferred type of a variable based on its name by checking a predefined map of type mappings, if the name is found in the map it returns the corresponding type, otherwise it falls back to capitalizing the first letter of the name."];
  "main.main" [tooltip="File: main.go:73\n\nThe function initializes a CallGraph data structure to analyze a directory specified by the user, which defaults to the current directory if not provided as a command-line flag '-dir'. It then initializes and caches information from the directory, performs analysis on the directory to populate the CallGraph, generates explanations based on the graph and cached information, and outputs the CallGraph in DOT format."];
  "Cache.Get" [tooltip="File: main.go:126\n\nThis function retrieves an explanation associated with a given hash from a database, returning the explanation as a string and a boolean indicating whether the retrieval was successful."];
  "main.hashSourceCode" [tooltip="File: main.go:144\n\nThis function generates a SHA-256 hash of the input code string, converting the result into a hexadecimal string representation for storage or comparison purposes."];
  "main.analyzeDirectory" [tooltip="File: main.go:149\n\nThe function analyzes a directory, traversing its contents recursively using filepath.Walk, and ignores files with suffix .go, _test.go, or those within the vendor/ directory, while calling the analyzeFile function on eligible Go source files to update the CallGraph."];
  "main.analyzeFile" [tooltip="File: main.go:165\n\nThis function analyzes the source code of a file specified by filename and populates a CallGraph structure with information about the code. It uses the Go parser to parse the file, creates an astVisitor instance to walk the Abstract Syntax Tree and extract relevant data, and finally reads the source file to provide raw code to the visitor."];
  "astVisitor.Visit" [tooltip="File: main.go:201\n\nThis method implements a visitation pattern for abstract syntax tree (AST) nodes, processing function declarations and function calls. It extracts relevant information from function declarations, storing it in a map of functions, while function calls are used to append call targets to the current function's call map."];
  "main.generateExplanations" [tooltip="File: main.go:329\n\nThis function generates AI explanations for a set of functions in a call graph. It checks if a GROQ API key is set, and if so, it loops through the call graph's functions, processing them in batches to generate explanations for each function's source code. The function uses a cache to store previous results to avoid repeated explanations. If an error occurs during explanation generation, the function logs the error and replaces the explanation with an empty string. The function returns no error if it cannot find any functions to process or if it successfully generates explanations for all functions."];
  "Cache.Set" [tooltip="File: main.go:135\n\nThis function sets a key-value pair in a database, specifically inserting or replacing an entry in the 'explanations' table with a hash and corresponding explanation string."];
  "Cache.Close" [tooltip="File: main.go:140\n\nThis function is a method on a Cache struct that closes the connection to the database, delegating the actual closing operation to the c.db.Close() method and returning any resulting error."];
  "astVisitor.extractSourceCode" [tooltip="File: main.go:237\n\nThis function extracts source code for a given function declaration as a string, returning the original source code if available, or formatted source code if not, using the go/format library as a fallback."];
  "main.callLLM" [tooltip="File: main.go:390\n\nThe function calls an LLM API with the provided apiKey and sourceCode as user input, generating a system prompt containing the code analysis rules and user prompt with the sourceCode. It then unmarshals and checks the API response for validity, returning a single message from the LLM's response if successful."];
  "main.outputDOT" [tooltip="File: main.go:455\n\nThis function generates a text-based DOT graph representing a call graph, where nodes represent functions and edges represent function calls. It includes each function's file information and explanation, if available, as a tooltip on hover. The function calls between functions are also represented by edges, provided both the caller and callee functions exist in the call graph."];
  "astVisitor.Visit" -> "astVisitor.getFunctionName";
  "astVisitor.Visit" -> "astVisitor.getReceiver";
  "astVisitor.Visit" -> "astVisitor.extractSourceCode";
  "astVisitor.Visit" -> "main.hashSourceCode";
  "astVisitor.Visit" -> "astVisitor.getCallTarget";
  "astVisitor.getCallTarget" -> "main.inferTypeFromVarName";
  "main.analyzeDirectory" -> "main.analyzeFile";
  "main.main" -> "main.initCache";
  "main.main" -> "Cache.Close";
  "main.main" -> "main.analyzeDirectory";
  "main.main" -> "main.generateExplanations";
  "main.main" -> "main.outputDOT";
  "astVisitor.getFunctionName" -> "astVisitor.getReceiver";
  "main.generateExplanations" -> "Cache.Get";
  "main.generateExplanations" -> "main.callLLM";
  "main.generateExplanations" -> "Cache.Set";
}
